Journal page: dated entries in plain prose
title end

paragraph start
Use a journal page to write what happened and what you learned, one section per day or topic. Put the date or the topic in each section title.
paragraph end

section start
title start
First section
title end

paragraph start
Write what happened, what you decided and what you learned, in plain sentences. Do not tidy it. A later reader needs the facts and the reason more than good style.
paragraph end

section end

